TraceBuffer stores enabled flag, generation, bounded events and dropped count.
begin(receiver, message) -> generation
  If enabled and not control traffic, record sender, receiver, arguments, chain,
  start time and running state; discard oldest beyond 1000 entries.
finish(generation, reply)
  Complete the matching event with result/signal, timestamp and elapsed duration.
  Ignore completions after clear or replacement of the trace generation.
configure(start/stop/clear)
  Start clears and enables; stop disables new entries; clear invalidates history.
snapshot -> copied event list, enabled flag and dropped count.
Coordinator start/stop/clear applies to all registered objects; registering objects
join active tracing before spawn completion. Object failures remain individually visible.
GET /trace aggregates events in time order, with optional receiver and chain filters.
POST /trace controls collection. Object messages __trace: and __traceJson expose
the same records. Historical references do not keep objects alive.
